Core Principles of GitOps

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing from my Ansible series, I’ve now started exploring GitOps as part of my ongoing DevOps learning journey! 💻☁️

Let’s dive into the core principles that make GitOps powerful:
1️⃣ Version Control
Git acts as the single source of truth for infrastructure and applications.
Every change is tracked and can be rolled back easily.

2️⃣ Declarative Configuration
Define your desired state in YAML manifests.
The system automatically enforces the desired state, reducing manual errors.

3️⃣ Automation
Deployments, updates, and monitoring are automated via controllers.
Reduces human intervention and improves efficiency.

4️⃣ Continuous Reconciliation
GitOps tools continuously compare actual state vs desired state.
Any drift is automatically corrected to match the Git repository.

💡 Fun Fact: GitOps brings developer-friendly CI/CD practices to infrastructure management!
